  "_comment": [
    "A worked, working example of the firmforge repository convention.",
    "",
    "Every part below points at ESP32 Marauder's own GitHub release assets rather",
    "than a copy stored here. That is deliberate: referencing upstream means no",
    "redistribution takes place, so no licence obligation is inherited, and the",
    "SHA-256 values become a genuine integrity check on someone else's artifact",
    "instead of a checksum of our own copy. See plan/spec/legal-and-licensing.md.",
    "",
    "Offsets, sizes and digests are copied verbatim from Marauder's authoritative",
    "installer manifest (firmware-manifest.json, v1.14.1, commit 43aa8bc1), which",
    "is generated from Arduino CLI's real upload recipe rather than guessed.",
    "",
    "Marauder is MIT licensed. It is offensive-security tooling: use it only on",
    "networks you own or are authorised to test."
  ],

